# Controller Inheritance Contract

## Normal case

A surface-local `ApplicationController` is the normal parent for authentication-aware endpoints. It
carries the app-wide authentication, authorization, preference, actor, and other lifecycle
callbacks.

## The BareController exception

`BareController` is the explicit exception: it must inherit directly from `ActionController::Base`,
never from `ApplicationController`. Bare endpoints intentionally bypass the app-wide lifecycle
callbacks and are expected to declare any protections they need directly on `BareController`.

## Do not normalize

Do not "normalize" `BareController` inheritance to `ApplicationController`. Doing so silently
re-attaches the full lifecycle to endpoints that were deliberately built to be self-defending and
bare. If a bare endpoint needs a protection, declare it on `BareController`, do not change its
parent.
